#!/usr/bin/env python3
# bromigos:summary=The desktop panels: run them (login does), show or hide one or all, edit mode, type in the notes
# bromigos:args=[toggle NAME|all | show NAME|all | add NAME | edit [on|done|cancel] | notes | reload | gallery [--previews DIR]]
"""Bromigos desktop widgets: SYSTEM, NETWORK, STORAGE, WORKBENCH, FIELD NOTES, SHORTCUTS (and LAB and the
homelab's declared panels with bromigos-homelab: plugins).

One GTK3 process, one layer-shell surface per panel on the BOTTOM layer (above any
background/live layer, below windows) of its own monitor: the one its layout.json entry's
"output" names (by make, model and serial, else connector), else the primary. A panel
whose monitor isn't connected shows on the primary, and goes back when it returns.

  bromigos-widgets                 run (Hyprland login autostart)
  bromigos-widgets toggle NAME     show/hide one panel (system|network|storage|lab|workbench|shortcuts|notes)
  bromigos-widgets toggle all      hide/restore the visible panels
  bromigos-widgets show NAME|all   show one panel or every one (never hides; the app launcher's
                                   Desktop Panels entry), starting the panels if they aren't running
  bromigos-widgets add NAME        show a panel in a free spot on the desktop, and save it there
  bromigos-widgets edit [on|done|cancel]
                                   edit mode: move, resize and switch the panels on the desktop
                                   (no word: on, or done when it's on; starts the panels first)
  bromigos-widgets gallery [--previews DIR]
                                   every panel there is, as JSON (the widget gallery's list);
                                   --previews draws each to DIR/<name>.png
  bromigos-widgets notes           focus FIELD NOTES for typing (Esc hands focus back; starts the
                                   panels first if they aren't running: the Field Notes entry)
  bromigos-widgets reload          re-read layout.json
  bromigos-widgets stats           print draw counts and coverage to the app's stderr
  bromigos-widgets render NAME|plugins/x.py OUT.png [--ticks N] [--size WxH]
                                   draw one panel to a PNG offscreen (no window; real readings;
                                   --size: at that size, in the layout of its size class there)

Plugins: plugins/<name>.py defines a Panel subclass; it is picked up, hot-reloaded and
isolated by plugins.py (see its docstring). Health: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/bromigos-widgets-health.json.

Redraws pause while the active workspace on a panel's monitor has tiled or
fullscreen windows covering the desktop; sampling continues (cheaply) so the
waterfall and scope have history when you come back.
"""
